{"resultsPerPage":689,"startIndex":32000,"totalResults":32689,"format":"NVD_CVE","version":"2.0","timestamp":"2026-10-24T11:54:23.113","vulnerabilities":[{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-114136","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-10-21T20:17:25.557","lastModified":"2026-10-22T17:21:57.293","vulnStatus":"Awaiting Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Django REST framework is a toolkit for building Web APIs. From 3.6.4 until 3.18.2, JSONParser.parse in rest_framework/parsers.py uses the client-supplied Content-Type charset value with codecs.getreader, which accepts byte-transform codecs such as bz2_codec rather than only text encodings. A remote unauthenticated client can therefore cause a compressed JSON request body to be expanded after Django has enforced DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE against only the wire bytes, allowing a very small request to consume substantial per-worker memory. The default parser set is sufficient, and any reachable endpoint that accepts a JSON body is affected. This issue is fixed in version 3.18.2."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"encode","product":"django-rest-framework","versions":[{"version":">= 3.6.4, < 3.18.2","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","baseScore":7.5,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"NONE","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"NONE","integrityImpact":"NONE","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-409"},{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-770"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/encode/django-rest-framework/commit/3c2634599b26a9f789b03045118dbc276117611a","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/encode/django-rest-framework/releases/tag/3.18.2","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/encode/django-rest-framework/security/advisories/GHSA-3547-9m27-7rxg","source":"security-advisories@github.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-114138","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-10-21T21:17:56.200","lastModified":"2026-10-22T17:34:37.867","vulnStatus":"Awaiting Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Django REST framework is a toolkit for building Web APIs. Prior to 3.18.2, DefaultContentNegotiation.get_accept_list in rest_framework/negotiation.py accepts an unbounded number and aggregate size of Accept tokens, while select_renderer in that file repeatedly invokes _MediaType parsing from rest_framework/utils/mediatypes.py for each attacker-controlled token, every renderer, and forced 406 renegotiation. A remote unauthenticated client can send many distinct media types containing large quoted parameter values with numerous semicolons, causing Django's parameter parser and DRF's repeated parsing structure to consume disproportionate CPU. Requests to any reachable endpoint can pin synchronous workers for prolonged periods, and concurrent requests can make the service unavailable until the requests stop. This issue is fixed in version 3.18.2."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"encode","product":"django-rest-framework","versions":[{"version":"< 3.18.2","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","baseScore":7.5,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"NONE","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"NONE","integrityImpact":"NONE","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-400"},{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-407"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/encode/django-rest-framework/commit/148ab6523922d5a0c110f76615935e5220b63029","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/encode/django-rest-framework/releases/tag/3.18.2","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/encode/django-rest-framework/security/advisories/GHSA-33wh-fxxf-88vv","source":"security-advisories@github.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-96636","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-10-21T21:20:31.760","lastModified":"2026-10-22T16:46:48.920","vulnStatus":"Undergoing Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Pillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 13.0.0, MpoImageFile.seek() and DcxImageFile.seek() reparse later MPO or DCX frames and replace self._size without rerunning Image._decompression_bomb_check(). A crafted multi-frame image can use a tiny first frame to pass Image.open() and then declare an over-limit later frame. Normal frame iteration through seek(), load(), or ImageSequence.Iterator can decode that frame and commit hundreds of megabytes or more, causing memory-exhaustion denial of service. This issue is fixed in version 13.0.0."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"python-pillow","product":"Pillow","versions":[{"version":"< 13.0.0","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","baseScore":6.5,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"NONE","userInteraction":"REQUIRED","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"NONE","integrityImpact":"NONE","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":2.8,"impactScore":3.6}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-400"},{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-409"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/f1acfc54c53502948d0d14121872061df931db48","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/pull/10011","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/releases/tag/13.0.0","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/security/advisories/GHSA-p8hx-v2p6-rp84","source":"security-advisories@github.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-96638","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-10-21T21:20:32.067","lastModified":"2026-10-22T16:46:48.920","vulnStatus":"Undergoing Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Pillow is a Python imaging library. From 9.1.0 until 13.0.0, BmpRleDecoder.decode() in src/PIL/BmpImagePlugin.py permits crafted RLE BMP delta escapes and absolute-mode runs to append beyond the remaining dest_length without a per-branch cap. A delta can add roughly 255 image rows in one iteration, so a kilobyte-sized file with a large but permitted width can expand the data bytearray to hundreds of megabytes or more, causing memory-exhaustion denial of service. This issue is fixed in version 13.0.0."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"python-pillow","product":"Pillow","versions":[{"version":">= 9.1.0, < 13.0.0","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","baseScore":6.5,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"NONE","userInteraction":"REQUIRED","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"NONE","integrityImpact":"NONE","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":2.8,"impactScore":3.6}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-400"},{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-770"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/e7794835e323ff2691d9b3a974cade1a44301b9a","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/pull/10015","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/releases/tag/13.0.0","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/security/advisories/GHSA-24rc-8hj2-v98c","source":"security-advisories@github.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-96640","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-10-21T21:20:32.357","lastModified":"2026-10-22T16:46:48.920","vulnStatus":"Undergoing Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Pillow is a Python imaging library. From 5.1.0 until 13.0.0, PdfParser.linearize_page_tree() in src/PIL/PdfParser.py treats a PDF /Pages graph as a tree without tracking duplicate indirect references. When Image.save(..., format=\"PDF\", append=True) processes an attacker-controlled existing PDF whose /Kids arrays repeatedly reference the same child /Pages node, Pillow expands the shared subtree as distinct pages. A compact malformed PDF can therefore create exponentially many page references and consume disproportionate CPU before the append completes. This issue is fixed in version 13.0.0."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"python-pillow","product":"Pillow","versions":[{"version":">= 5.1.0, < 13.0.0","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV40":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvs